From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:11:46 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: soc: apple: Add the T6040 AOP

The T6040 (M4 Pro) AOP starts like the T6020 one, through RTKit over a
single mailbox with patched boot arguments, not through the T8140 setup
port. Its firmware's external code and log segments must be mapped into
the AOP's DART again before the start, from /reserved-memory nodes the
bootloader adds. Describe the node with its four register windows, as
Apple's device tree lists them (the driver uses the SRAM and the ASC
wrapper), and its audio, ambient light and lid angle service children.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
